  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Primary path and call ownership",
      "items": [
        "Highlighted arrows follow one selected master \u2192 branch business event. Both sites run the same app; this is a runtime overview, not a synchronous call stack.",
        "api/events.py:18\u201338 calls ingest() and returns receipts. delivery.py:103\u2013108 later calls execute_captures() and refresh_results(). The API does not execute business application.",
        "The receiver runner reads inbox rows; logical outbox/inbox DocTypes live in the per-site databases."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "What actually triggers a dispatch",
      "items": [
        "hooks.py:17\u201329 registers document lifecycle callbacks. outbox.py:15\u201324 requires enabled streaming, Master/Slave role, eligible DocType and no trusted replay or install/migration context.",
        "outbox.py:67\u201392 selects event flags, rule direction, Branch and conditions from committed configuration. policy.py:104\u2013127 handles Both and separate reverse conditions. Missing required Branch is rejected.",
        "outbox.py:135\u2013136 suppresses duplicate insert/submit callbacks; 174\u2013180 suppresses unchanged snapshots. on_submit maps to an Update carrying document state."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Transaction and immutable payload",
      "items": [
        "outbox.py:195\u2013228 projects linked associations per peer and groups matching payloads. 244\u2013287 freezes files/dependencies, inserts Dispatch Event and registers an after-commit wakeup without committing the business transaction.",
        "Source changes and their dispatch roll back together. transport.py:43\u201367 selects due, unacknowledged destination rows in event sequence and verifies pairing generation.",
        "MariaDB holds business, event, receipt, immutable-version and checkpoint state independently for each site."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Peer and execution trust boundaries",
      "items": [
        "delivery.py:77\u201382 requires an enabled Connected peer and synchronized policy before transport. client.py:15\u201345 uses HTTPS-only normalized URLs, dedicated credentials, bounded requests and no redirects.",
        "auth.py:51\u2013104 restricts credentials to wire endpoints. inbox.py:15\u201370 validates envelope, source/pairing/generation, captured rule, Branch and duplicate digest.",
        "context.py:13\u201324 switches replay to an enabled non-Administrator local user. executor.py:38\u201380 enforces duplicate policy, permissions, mappings and conflict base; 198\u2013210 uses normal save/insert/submit/cancel. Frames show logical trust domains, not inferred network firewalls."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Execution ordering and delivery results",
      "items": [
        "executor.py:352\u2013363 pauses normal slave replay during an In Progress/Failed bootstrap. 397\u2013424 coalesces rename identities, chooses the earliest pending event per record and then the earliest due head; it is not one global FIFO blocking every record.",
        "executor.py:424\u2013452 commits successful application and capture status together; failures roll back business effects and persist backoff. Independent records can continue.",
        "transport.py:71\u2013102 marks durable delivery. feedback.py:116\u2013182 separately fetches receiver outcomes. feedback.py:99\u2013113 retries the existing failed capture; Delivered does not mean Applied."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Supporting dependencies and alternate paths",
      "items": [
        "agent.py:16\u201340 runs supervised per-peer passes, default interval one second. delivery.py:127\u2013146 uses a Redis peer lock. tasks.py:4\u201345 queues recovery jobs; hooks.py:30\u201333 schedules minute recovery and daily retention. These are configured intervals, not measured latency.",
        "Frappe/ERPNext supply HTTP routing, controllers, permissions and document storage; Redis and Frappe workers support scheduling. Per-site Redis services are described here to keep the canvas focused.",
        "delivery.py:85\u201387 advances Copy Runs before exchange. transport.py:105\u2013140 lets branch agents push outgoing events and pull incoming master events, committing local receipt before remote acknowledgement. The highlighted route shows direct master push.",
        "This diagram is derived from the cited code at the pinned revision. No live deployment, latency or business acceptance test was performed."
      ]
    }
  ]
